",\"background\":\"#4dc9f61a\",\"border\":\"1px solid #4dc9f640\"},\"children\":\"Legend\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankCardH3\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Tigreal\",\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L40\",null,{\"href\":\"/tier-list?rank=legend\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[11px] font-heading uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-text-accent hover:text-text-accent-bright transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankTierListLink\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}],\" →\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-muted text-[13px] leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceLead\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\",\"name\":\"Tigreal\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"45.37\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid1\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"Tigreal\",\"delta\":\"+0.51%\"}}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"2.39\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceMid2\"}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"text-text-primary\",\"children\":[\"8.15\",\"%\"]}],[\"$\",\"$L4c\",null,{\"k\":\"pages.heroes.rankSentenceAfter\",\"params\":{\"rank\":\"Legend\"}}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"article\",\"mythic\",{\"className\":\"group relative min-w-0 border border-mlbb-gold/15 bg-surface-1/40 p-3.5 pl-5 md:p-4 md:pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-mlbb-gold/30\",\"children\":[\"$La1\",\"$La2\",\"$La3\"]}],\"$La4\",\"$La5\"]}]\n7e:[\"$\",\"$L40\",\"a-0\",{\"href\":\"/patch-notes\",\"prefetch\":false,\"className\":\"text-[#C8AA6E] hover:text-[#F0D060] underline decoration-[#C8AA6E]/40 hover:decoration-[#F0D060] transition-colors\",\"children\":\"patch notes\"}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"If you cannot answer one question before locking him, do not pick him: when Implosion lands, which two enemy heroes are supposed to die first?\"}]\n80:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"His whole kit is a delivery system for one pull\"]}]\n81:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-5\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Tigreal is not a \\\"combo tank\\\" in the generic sense. He is a delivery system for one reliable pull, and the rest of the kit only exists to make that pull matter.\"}]\n82:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-6\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Attack Wave is not a poke button. It is the spell that slows the exit route after you have already claimed space. Sacred Hammer is not mobility for its own sake. It is the tool that changes enemy positioning before your team commits damage. Even his passive matters because it blocks one incoming basic attack after enough stacks, which means he gets a small but real buffer when walking into marksman fire, turret shots, or jungle skirmishes.\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-7\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Once you understand that, Tigreal becomes much easier to pilot correctly. You stop obsessing over landing a five-man montage set and start playing for one controlled displacement. Sometimes that means Sacred Hammering a jungler away from Retribution range. Sometimes it means pulling only the enemy mage and marksman while leaving the tank outside the fight. The hero works when you treat crowd control as geometry, not spectacle.\"}]\n84:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-8\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"His biggest weakness is also why he stays relevant. Everybody knows what he wants to do, but not every draft can physically stop it. If the enemy must hold a cancel, a Purify, or a Diggie ultimate every time you disappear into fog, you are already controlling the pace even before the engage happens.\"}]\n85:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-2\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Roaming the first 6 minutes\"]}]\n86:[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Take Sacred Hammer first and play the lane edge, not the buff center.\"}],\" Level 1 Tigreal matters because his push changes where the first skirmish happens. Stand on the side of the wave or jungle entrance that lets you shove a target toward your team, not away from them. If you walk straight into the enemy buff camp with no lane priority, you are donating HP for nothing.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Touch the mid wave, then leave immediately.\"}],\" Your first clear is about mid priority, not about staying for experience. Show for one wave, help your mage secure space with Attack Wave once you have it, then move to the nearest brush that threatens the enemy jungler's second camp or the gold lane river entrance. Tigreal wins early minutes by making carries nervous, not by sitting in lane.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Save Flicker unless the first cast wins a crab, a buff reset, or first blood.\"}],\" Flicker is the spell that turns his engage from obvious to unavoidable. Spending it for a low-value poke play before the first turtle hands the enemy a long window of freedom. Spend it only when the result changes the map immediately. If not, keep the threat alive and let the enemy waste positioning around a cooldown you still own.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n87:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-3\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"The spike you are farming toward\"]}]\n88:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-9\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":[\"Tigreal's real two-item spike is \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Tough Boots with Conceal unlocked plus Dominance Ice\"}],\", usually in the 7 to 9 minute window if your roam gold is flowing correctly.\"]}]\n89:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-10\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Before that threshold, he is honest. Everybody sees the angle, everybody sees the walk-up, and even if you find the flank you are still fragile enough to get punished on the exit. After that threshold, two things change at once. Conceal gives you the invisible entry angle and movement burst that lets you start fights from outside normal reaction distance. Dominance Ice makes the first response from the enemy backline weaker: its Fortress Shield and Lifebane passives work as a short-range aura, cutting the shield and HP regen of every enemy who stays close to you, so the trade after the set leans your way.\"}]\n8a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-11\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"That combination is what turns Tigreal from a visible frontliner into a real fight starter. You stop asking whether you can reach the enemy carry and start asking whether the enemy carry has already stepped too far forward to escape. The mechanical change is simple: you can now enter through fog, absorb the first counter hit, and still have enough durability left to finish the sequence.\"}]\n8b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-12\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"If your composition does not need stealth angles and mostly fights front to back, Encourage can replace Conceal later. But the first true ranked spike is still the same idea: completed roam boots plus Dominance Ice. That is the moment you should stop drifting through the map and start forcing your presence into every objective setup.\"}]\n8c:[\"$\",\"$La6\",null,{\"slot\":\"7246933188\",\"variant\":\"in-article\",\"className\":\"my-8\"}]\n8d:[[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-0\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Teamfight positioning and target priority\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The wrong reflex on Tigreal is to hold everything for the dream five-man ultimate. That reflex throws games because the enemy backline only needs one answer to ruin a greedy engage.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The right reflex is to catch the fight where it is weakest. If the enemy mage and marksman are stacked on one side of the choke, take those two. If their assassin is diving your carry, peel first and turn the fight after. Tigreal wins more games from a clean two-man catch on the correct heroes than from a desperate swing at all five.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",\"ol-0\",{\"className\":\"list-decimal list-inside text-[#9BA0B4] my-3 space-y-2 ml-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Flank from a side brush, not from the center line.\"}],\" Walking straight through the tank line tells the enemy exactly what is coming. Coming from a side angle forces their backline to choose between burning movement early or holding position and risking the pull.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-1\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"Start closer to the carries than to the tank.\"}],\" If your first contact is the enemy EXP or roamer, you are already late. Your body should be positioned where Sacred Hammer threatens the damage dealers. Tigreal is not there to win a frontliner duel.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"li-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"strong-0\",{\"className\":\"text-[#E8E6E3] font-semibold\",\"children\":\"After Implosion, push toward your team, not deeper into theirs.\"}],\" The second cast of Sacred Hammer is where good Tigreal players cash the engage in. If you knock targets away from your own damage, the setup was wasted. Finish the combo by collapsing the fight toward your side of the map.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-2\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The edge case is double-support style drafts. If your team has Angela attached to a carry comp, you can spend Flicker more aggressively because Heartguard covers the first punish window after you commit. If your sustain angle is Estes instead, you need to re-center faster after the set so the fight stays inside his healing field. Same hero, different follow-through.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h2\",\"h2-1\",{\"className\":\"text-xl md:text-[26px] font-heading font-bold text-[#F0D060] mt-10 mb-4 first:mt-0 text-balance uppercase tracking-[0.04em] leading-tight relative\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"className\":\"block w-10 h-[3px] bg-gradient-to-r from-[#F0D060] to-[#C8AA6E]/0 mb-3\"}],\"Itemization: locked slots and real conversations\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-3\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"Tigreal does not need a \\\"build order\\\" as much as he needs two locked slots and several honest conversations.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"p-4\",{\"className\":\"text-[#9BA0B4] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-[15px]\",\"children\":\"The locked slots are your roam boots and Dominance Ice. Boots decide how you start fights. Dominance Ice is the default first major armor buy because its aura matters in every real engagement. Tough Boots is the normal choice into heavy control because the reduced CC and slow duration helps you finish your sequence. Warrior Boots is the better lane-to-lane start into basic-attack-heavy physical comps that chip you on entry. Rapid Boots is for snowballing maps where movement speed matters more than combat stats and you are playing vision games rather than face-tanking.\"}],\"\\n\",\"$La7\",\"\\n\",\"$La8\",\"\\n\",\"$La9\",\"\\n\",\"$Laa\",\"\\n\",\"$Lab\",\"\\n\",\"$Lac\",\"\\n\",\"$Lad\",\"\\n\",\"$Lae\",\"\\n\",\"$Laf\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb0\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb1\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb2\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb3\",\"\\n\",\"$Lb4\"]\n8e:[\"$\",\"$Lb5\",null,{\"heroName\":\"Tigreal\"}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"8f:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative bg-surface-4 border border-mlbb-gold/20 overflow-hidden card-hover hover:border-mlbb-gold/50\",\"style\":{\"boxS